OSF brand guidelines: licence scope index

Copyright 2026 Open Science Stiftung (Open Science Foundation), except where
another rights holder is identified. Grants apply only to rights the relevant
licensor is authorised to grant.

1. Prose and documentation: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International.
   Full unmodified text: LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.
2. Implementation files, tokens, CSS, recipes, skills and agent instructions:
   Apache License, Version 2.0. Full unmodified text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
3. Logo and wordmark artwork: LicenseRef-OSF-Brand-Assets, a limited,
   non-open permission. Full text: LICENSES/LicenseRef-OSF-Brand-Assets.txt.
   TRADEMARK.md explains trademark use and the distinction from copyright.

Per-file SPDX notices and REUSE.toml define the exact scope. The root index does
not grant an additional or alternative licence. Unknown files must receive an
explicit classification before being committed. Licence texts are reproduced
as legal instruments; they are not relicensed as repository implementation code.

CC BY and Apache do not license the OSF marks for branding a derivative work.
Trademark policy does not revoke or narrow the separate CC BY or Apache grants,
or rights and exceptions available independently under applicable law.

Commercial fonts, photographs and the original Office kit are absent. No rights
in those external materials are granted. See docs/external-assets.md.

Private GitHub visibility controls access. It does not revoke the licences
already granted to recipients or impose confidentiality on licensed material.
